---
title: How to set Trigger For Email Sequence?
sidebar:
  order: 17
---
To automate your email sequence based on specific deal events, follow these steps to set a trigger in Taskip.

#### **Step 1: Open the Sales Pipeline**

1. Navigate to the Dashboard.
1. Click on Sales Pipeline from the left sidebar.

#### **Step 2: Open the Deal’s Email Sequence**

1. Click on the deal name to open its details.
1. Select the Email Sequence tab.

![](./how-to-set-trigger-for-email-sequence/content/image-12-1024x475.png)

#### **Step 3: Update the Email Sequence Trigger**

1. Click on “Update Sequence” in the top-right corner.
1. The Update Email Sequence modal will appear.

#### **Step 4: Select a Trigger Type**

1. Click on the **Trigger Type** dropdown menu.
1. Choose one of the following triggers:
   - **Deal Created Date** – Triggers emails based on when the deal was created.
   - **Deal Closed Date** – Starts the sequence after the deal is closed.
   - **Deal Stage Change** – Triggers emails when the deal moves to a new stage.
   - **Deal Task Complete** – Starts when a task associated with the deal is marked complete.
   - **Deal Meeting Complete** – Sends emails after a scheduled meeting is completed.
   - **Custom Date** – Allows manual scheduling of the sequence.

![](./how-to-set-trigger-for-email-sequence/content/image-11-1.png)

#### **Step 5: Save Changes**

1. After selecting the desired trigger, click “**Update**” to save the settings.
1. The sequence will now start based on the selected event.

Your email sequence is now set to trigger automatically based on deal activity!

